---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base='https://zyyang0124.github.io/MimicryDB/api';
const endpoints=[
 {method:'GET',path:'/api/interactions.json',desc:'Every interaction record with its claim-level references (the atomic edges).'},
 {method:'GET',path:'/api/interactions/MIMICRY-000001.json',desc:'One interaction by stable ID (colon replaced by a dash), plus its references and systems.'},
 {method:'GET',path:'/api/taxa.json',desc:'Taxon directory with per-role record counts.'},
 {method:'GET',path:'/api/taxa/cuculus-canorus.json',desc:'Taxon research profile: roles, models/mimics, modalities, types, evidence profile, interactions, systems.'},
 {method:'GET',path:'/api/references.json',desc:'Reference list with per-reference support counts.'},
 {method:'GET',path:'/api/systems.json · /api/systems/SYSTEM-000001.json',desc:'Mimicry systems (rings/complexes) and their member interactions.'},
 {method:'GET',path:'/api/ontology.json',desc:'All controlled vocabularies with stable term IDs (TERM:<VOCABULARY>:<TERM>), hierarchy and definitions. Ontology v1.1.'},
];
const sbExample=`curl "https://ylrtwccsnzeckrfhqpbt.supabase.co/rest/v1/mimicry_interaction?select=public_id,mimicry_summary&interaction_status=eq.published" -H "apikey: <SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY>"`;
---
<Layout title="Public API · MimicryDB"><div class="container py-12"><span class="pill">READ-ONLY · CC BY 4.0</span><h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold">Public API</h1>
<p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-slate-400">Two complementary read-only interfaces. The static JSON API is versioned with every site build (no credentials, cacheable, citable per release). The Supabase REST endpoint is <em>live</em> and filterable via PostgREST syntax — its data is whatever has passed curation review.</p>

<h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">1 · Static JSON API</h2>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Generated at build time from the same DataProvider the site renders. Regenerated on every commit; cite a release for stability.</p>
<div class="mt-6 space-y-3">{endpoints.map(e=><div class="card text-sm"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-3"><span class="pill">{e.method}</span><code class="text-gold">{e.path}</code></div><p class="mt-2 text-slate-400">{e.desc}</p></div>)}</div>
<p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">CORS note: GitHub Pages does not send CORS headers — browser fetches from other origins will fail; server-side and CLI use work fine (curl/wget). For in-browser cross-origin analysis, use the Supabase endpoint below.</p>

<h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">2 · Live Supabase REST (filterable)</h2>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">PostgREST with row-level security: only <code>interaction_status='published'</code> rows are visible. The publishable key is public by design.</p>
<pre class="card mt-4 overflow-x-auto p-4 text-xs text-white/90">{sbExample}</pre>
<p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">Filters compose: <code>&evidence_grade=in.(E2,E3)&amp;mimic_taxon_id=not.is.null</code>. Full OpenAPI schema at <code>/rest/v1/</code>.</p>

<h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Terms</h2>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Data: <a class="underline" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a> — cite <em>MimicryDB (2026), github.com/ZyYang0124/MimicryDB</em>. Until v1.0 all records are labeled demo data; the API shape is already the v1.0 contract.</p>
</div></Layout>
